{
  "what": "Sommelier V1+ P7 (fallback): V1 without its model with the fallback part on (engine v1-fallback: createSommelierFallback, else plain() via createSommelierService with llm = null) against V1 without its model today (engine v1-basic). Free: no model was called.",
  "caveats": [
    "Evidence for the owner, not a quality claim (D-50).",
    "The scenarios and their labels (which wines are good, ok or poor for a dish) were written by an AI, not by people.",
    "holdout-dev is no longer unseen: its failures were read in S9 and rules answer to some of them.",
    "holdout-test is blind: its vectors are keyed by a salted hash (SOMMELIER_EVAL_BLIND_SALT, not committed) and it is reported in totals only.",
    "The engines are deterministic: one run per engine and set; the intervals are over dishes (clusters), not runs.",
    "Latency is wall-clock on a shared 4-core development machine with in-memory stand-ins for the database reads; production adds the reads of the engines (profiles, taste) and the engines' rate-limit check."
